### [K] CompositionOrder.lean:348 finiteOrderOn_of_stagePreserving
doc CompositionOrder.lean:345-347:
  | /-- **Finite order from stage preservation.** A reversible datum that respects affine relations
  | and carries each stage's preparations to preparation vectors of the same stage induces an
  | automorphism of finite order on the chart body. -/
  > theorem finiteOrderOn_of_stagePreserving {S T : OpDatum D} (hS : AffineRespect S)
  >     (hT : AffineRespect T) (hST : Undoes C S T hS) (hTS : Undoes C T S hT)
  >     (hsp : StagePreserving T) :
  >     FiniteOrderOn (chartBody C) (inducedEquiv C hS hT hST hTS) :=

### [K] CompositionOrder.lean:109 not_ordInf_of_finite_of_mulClosed
doc CompositionOrder.lean:106-108:
  | /-- **Closure control.** A finite composition-closed set of affine automorphisms has no member of
  | infinite order on any set: the composites of a member with itself stay in the set, two of them
  | coincide, and cancellation gives a positive power fixing everything. -/
  > theorem not_ordInf_of_finite_of_mulClosed {Ω : Set V} {G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)} (hG : G.Finite)
  >     (hcl : MulClosed G) : ¬ OrdInf Ω G :=

### [K] CompositionOrder.lean:456 ord1_core
doc CompositionOrder.lean:452-455:
  | /-- **Round ORD-1.** A reversible stage-preserving datum induces an automorphism of finite order
  | on the chart body; a reversible datum of infinite order has every positive power nontrivial; the
  | rotation by one radian has infinite order on the ball; the Householder set has no member of
  | infinite order; the singleton of the rotation has one; a finite composition-closed set has none. -/
  > theorem ord1_core :
  >     (∀ (D : DirectedStages) (C : CompletionChart D) (S T : OpDatum D) (hS : AffineRespect S)
  >       (hT : AffineRespect T) (hST : Undoes C S T hS) (hTS : Undoes C T S hT),
  >         StagePreserving T → FiniteOrderOn (chartBody C) (inducedEquiv C hS hT hST hTS)) ∧
  >     (∀ (D : DirectedStages) (C : CompletionChart D) (S T : OpDatum D) (hS : AffineRespect S)
  >       (hT : AffineRespect T) (hST : Undoes C S T hS) (hTS : Undoes C T S hT),
  >         InfiniteOrderOn (chartBody C) (inducedEquiv C hS hT hST hTS) →
  >           ∀ m : ℕ, 1 ≤ m → ∃ x, (iterAfter C T hT m).τ x ≠ prepVec D x) ∧
  >     InfiniteOrderOn ball3 (rot3 1) ∧ ¬ OrdInf ball3 householder3 ∧ OrdInf ball3 {rot3 1} ∧
  >     (∀ (V : Type) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℝ V] (Ω : Set V) (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)),
  >       G.Finite → MulClosed G → ¬ OrdInf Ω G) :=

### [K] InvariantInnerProduct.lean:336 invariant_inner_product
doc InvariantInnerProduct.lean:332-335:
  | /-- **The invariant inner product.** On a compact body with nonempty interior, `invMatrix Ω` is
  | symmetric and positive definite, and every affine automorphism preserving the body fixes its
  | centroid and preserves the inner product `⟨u, v⟩ = u ⬝ᵥ (invMatrix Ω *ᵥ v)` through its linear
  | part. -/
  > theorem invariant_inner_product {Ω : Set (Fin n → ℝ)} (hc : IsCompact Ω)
  >     (hi : (interior Ω).Nonempty) :
  >     (invMatrix Ω)ᵀ = invMatrix Ω ∧ (∀ u, u ≠ 0 → 0 < u ⬝ᵥ (invMatrix Ω *ᵥ u)) ∧
  >       ∀ g : (Fin n → ℝ) ≃ᵃ[ℝ] (Fin n → ℝ), g '' Ω = Ω →
  >         g (centroid Ω) = centroid Ω ∧
  >           ∀ u v, (linMatrix g *ᵥ u) ⬝ᵥ (invMatrix Ω *ᵥ (linMatrix g *ᵥ v)) =
  >             u ⬝ᵥ (invMatrix Ω *ᵥ v) :=

### [K] InvariantInnerProduct.lean:152 centroid_fixed
doc InvariantInnerProduct.lean:150-151:
  | /-- **The centroid is fixed** by every affine automorphism preserving a compact body of positive
  | volume. -/
  > theorem centroid_fixed {Ω : Set (Fin n → ℝ)} (hc : IsCompact Ω) (hpos : 0 < volume.real Ω)
  >     (g : (Fin n → ℝ) ≃ᵃ[ℝ] (Fin n → ℝ)) (hg : g '' Ω = Ω) :
  >     g (centroid Ω) = centroid Ω :=

### [K] CompositeInterface.lean:210 ProductData
doc CompositeInterface.lean:208-209:
  | /-- Product-state and product-effect data on a real carrier `V`: a bi-affine product-state map and a
  | bilinear product-effect pairing with the evaluation law `prodEff e f (prodState x y) = e x * f y`. -/
  > structure ProductData (dA dB : ℕ) (V : Type) [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] where

### [K] CompositeInterface.lean:223 PreComposite
doc CompositeInterface.lean:220-222:
  | /-- A pre-composite: product data together with a convex body `Ω` of the carrier that contains the
  | product states, on which every product of effects is an effect and the unit pairing is one. These are
  | the eight fields of the interface other than local tomography. -/
  > structure PreComposite (ΩA : Set (Fin dA → ℝ)) (ΩB : Set (Fin dB → ℝ)) (V : Type)
  >     [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] extends ProductData dA dB V where

### [K] CompositeInterface.lean:235 LocallyTomographic
doc CompositeInterface.lean:232-234:
  | /-- Local tomography of a pre-composite: two states of the body that agree on every product of
  | effects are equal. Stated as a predicate so that it can be asserted of a structure as a field and
  | refuted of another as a control. -/
  > def LocallyTomographic {ΩA : Set (Fin dA → ℝ)} {ΩB : Set (Fin dB → ℝ)} {V : Type}
  >     [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] (P : PreComposite ΩA ΩB V) : Prop :=

### [K] CompositeInterface.lean:243 Composite
doc CompositeInterface.lean:240-242:
  | /-- **The weak composite interface.** A pre-composite with local tomography as a field. The field
  | `lt` is a premise of the structure; it is not derived from the other eight fields anywhere in this
  | module, and §G exhibits a pre-composite for which it fails. -/
  > structure Composite (ΩA : Set (Fin dA → ℝ)) (ΩB : Set (Fin dB → ℝ)) (V : Type)
  >     [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] extends PreComposite ΩA ΩB V where

### [K] CompositeInterface.lean:445 JointReversible
doc CompositeInterface.lean:444-444:
  | /-- Joint reversible action: a family of affine automorphisms of the carrier preserving the body. -/
  > abbrev JointReversible (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)) : Prop :=

### [K] CompositeInterface.lean:332 condA_prodState
doc CompositeInterface.lean:331-331:
  | /-- **L9.** No signalling on products: the conditional state of a product is its first factor. -/
